# One whole checkpoint run in the W3 2x checkpoint's SHAPE 2 form: a Device Portal ETW capture
# opened first, the `2x-D` window-smoke run inside it, then a read-only server snapshot, then the
# gather. Consumed by checkpoint.sh (via `run-scenario.sh checkpoint 2x-D`).
#
# This is the tracked form of what .build/lab-runtime/c2p-orchestrate.sh was on 2026-09-09. Its
# whole content is the four names and two numbers below; the ORDER, the signals each step is
# waited on and the ceilings on those waits live in checkpoint.sh, which is where they can be
# tested.

# jobs/etw-smoke.env -- the five graphics-stack providers at level 5. Its DURATION must cover the
# run plus the settle plus the teardown; 150 s covers the ~2 min window-smoke lanes with margin,
# and checkpoint.sh reads that same DURATION to bound its own wait for the capture's DONE line.
ETW_JOB=smoke

# jobs/smoke-2x-D.env -- the run being observed.
SMOKE_JOB=2x-D

# Take the read-only RdpCoreTS/Operational snapshot afterwards (jobs/server-snapshot.env, through
# the relay). It is the host's own account of the connection the run just made, and it is taken
# LAST because it opens an RDP session of its own: run concurrently it would appear in the very
# connection digest it is being asked to read. 0 skips it.
SNAPSHOT=1

# How long to wait after the capture's socket opens before the run is launched. The 2026-09-09
# orchestrator used 10 s, and the first capture of that night (0 frames, 0 events) is why the wait
# exists at all: the events that matter are the ones at session establishment, and a run that
# dials while the subscription is still settling loses them.
SETTLE_SECONDS=10

# The evidence directory everything is gathered into, under .build/evidence/. It names the LANE;
# pass a dated name as checkpoint.sh's second argument to give one RUN its own directory
# (`run-scenario.sh checkpoint 2x-D checkpoint-20260910`), which also overrides the smoke job's
# BATCH so the run's own evidence log lands in the same place. A tracked definition should not
# have to be edited to run it twice.
BATCH=w3-2x-checkpoint
